    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d207">

                <pb facs="0245" n="1079" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1079"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/10817</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Sharp</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-11-20T21:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 20, 1918, 9 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 10 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5935. War Trade Board, Bureau of Enemy Trade [from McFadden]:</p>
                <p>No. 617. Referring to Department’s 6206 of October 13 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >November 8</hi>], your 425. French Government are in accord with your views
                    that decisions of enemy license conferences should become effective at once and
                    are advising their representatives in Washington and London to this effect.
                        McFadden.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sharp</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
